<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38780" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεύνακτοι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span>,
			οἱ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐνάζω</span>)
		name for the Helots who were adopted into their lords' places during the
		Messenian wars, <i><span class="en">
			Theopomp.Hist.
			166
		</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
			D.S.
			8
		</span></i><i><span class="en">
			<u>Fr.</u>
			21
		</span></i> writes <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπευνακταί</span></b> , and
		seems to identify them with the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθενίαι</span> (q. v.): <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεύνακτοι: οἱ
		παρθενίαι,</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπευνακταί: οἱ
			συγκοιμηταί.</span></div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>